From 94a807f6177f2af16f74c5110c0af400efbc36a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:41:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 26/36] drm/msm/dsi: support the TCL firmware-described host
 and PHY

The ACPI DSI host and 10 nm PHY use explicit platform resources and
firmware-node references instead of OF discovery.

Add guarded host/PHY matches, resource checks, reference-owned PHY
lookup and validated lane/endpoint parsing. Publish the PHY PLL clocks
with complete clkdev names, retain and clean provider state, and add
byte-clock OPPs with power-domain levels. Propagate initial
clock/runtime-PM failures and initialize cleanup state before fallible
setup. The board coordinator must supply regulators and graph
connections; this driver adaptation alone does not make the LT8911
bridge cold-startable.
